# beatmania IIDX 7th style (GCB44 VER. JAB), Konami 2002: as bmiidx7a-play.his.
# beatmania IIDX 7th style (Twinkle): a scripted game from the NVRAM bmiidx7a-boot leaves (backup
# RAM cleared). The device check runs to ~f3000; two coins on the title, 1P Start, a key at
# mode select (LIGHT7) and at music select (5.1.1.), then the first stage played with a fixed
# pattern: the seven keys in turn and turntable spins in both directions, STAGE FAILED. The
# stage plays DVD chapter 64 (the game sends three digits; MAME reads them as a Video CD's two).
# Hashes the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, against MAME (PLAN.md 21, TW-5).
game bmiidx7

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 3300 press "Coin 1" 8
at 3330 press "Coin 1" 8
at 4000 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 4300 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 4900 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
# the stage: a key every 9 frames, 1 to 7 in turn; a turntable spin every 120 frames
at 5300 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 4
at 5309 press "P1-2 (SW2)" 4
at 5318 press "P1-3 (SW3)" 4
at 5327 press "P1-4 (SW4)" 4
